{
  "$comment": [
    "Synonym dictionary for the deterministic matcher (§ Phase 4).",
    "Data, not code, so a non-developer can extend it without touching TypeScript.",
    "",
    "Each key maps to the label text portals actually use. Devanagari entries sit",
    "alongside English ones because government portals label bilingually and the",
    "matcher splits on '/' before comparing.",
    "",
    "Rules for editing:",
    "  - Add phrases, never remove taxonomy keys (§4 append-only).",
    "  - Lowercase; punctuation is stripped before comparison, so skip it.",
    "  - Prefer distinctive phrases. A synonym that overlaps another key's",
    "    synonyms creates ambiguity, and an ambiguous match is capped below the",
    "    auto-fill threshold rather than guessed at.",
    "  - Every entry needs a fixture test (CLAUDE.md rule 5)."
  ],
